	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg7015"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=402" title="View the profile of Callon">Callon</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Drolvarg Guardian<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 320<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/YaBBImages/avatars/opus.gif" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								Warpig<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=402"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
								<a href="mailto:murgen21@yahoo.com"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/email_sm.gif" alt="Email" title="Email" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=771.msg7015#msg7015"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=771.msg7015#msg7015">Re:Beers</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #2 on:</b> April 14, 2004, 12:30:42 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							Much like most liquor that comes in a plastic bottle, if your beer comes in a 40 oz., it&#039;s crap. &nbsp;<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Smileys/Rodcet/smiley1.gif" alt="Smiley" border="0" /><br /><br />Best Light - As in a pale colored lager such as most big American beers or a light beer like Bud Light, etc.? &nbsp;If you mean the latter, I don&#039;t have one. &nbsp;Light beer is a tool of Satan. &nbsp; :o &nbsp;But if you mean the former.... hmm.... Harp maybe. &nbsp;Sam Adams Spring Ale is also quite good.<br /><br />Best Dark - How dark is dark? &nbsp;I love New Castle Brown Ale. &nbsp;If we mean really dark beers like Guinness, eh, I drink them occasionally but I&#039;m not a big fan.<br /><br />Micros - Great Lakes Brewery&#039;s Dortmunder Gold is good. &nbsp;Big Meadows Pale Ale from the Shenandoah Valley, but I think I was biased because I was on vacation taking long hikes every day and really enjoying that beer in the evening. &nbsp;With micros I&#039;m definitely partial to pale ales. &nbsp;<br /><br />Top overall choices not counting little micros, more or less in order -- <br /><br />New Castle<br />Killian&#039;s<br />Sam Adams Spring Ale<br /><br />Also good: Labatt&#039;s, Heineken, Sam Adams Octoberfest, and many more. &nbsp;Also almost any beer that&#039;s FREE... :D<br /><br /><br /><br /> &nbsp; &nbsp;
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
